Cycle 1: High-Performance Rate-Limiting Logic Sanitization
	• Trigger: Discovered that multi-agent concurrent operations were triggering partial bypass leaks during high-stress testing intervals.
	• Objective: Ensure complete type safety and atomic security boundaries at the API caching interface.
	• Phases:
		○ Phase A — Type Coercion Audit: Found that Upstash Redis returns numeric fields as string structures. Standard JavaScript evaluations like "5" < 3 silently failed, bypassing active rate blocks. Fix: Built an explicit parseRedisNumber() coercion wrapper in lib/rate-limit.ts.
		○ Phase B — TTL Expiration Leakage: Found that the Redis Lua script only refreshed keys upon the initial transaction (newCount === 1). At month boundaries, keys silently expired, granting free accounts unlimited queries. Fix: Modified Lua routines to scan TTL == -1 and force precise timestamp boundary limits via explicit PEXPIRE commands.
		○ Phase C — Concurrent Quota Race Condition: Shuffled the execution hierarchy order of operations. Shifted the counter increment mutation layer to execute before the primary database transaction blocks (optimistic locking pattern). If the Lua script logs a quota violation exception, processing drops immediately, completely blocking unauthorized writes to Supabase.
	• Lifecycle Status: 🟢 ACTIVE & ENFORCED
